    "brief": "When a review/<N> push is refused as non-fast-forward, cloud_relay.sh fetches the ref, re-applies the same verdict commit on the fresh tip and pushes; it never forces. If the fresh tip already carries the same verdict for the same head it skips; it logs either case. After any push it reports the remote tip (git ls-remote origin refs/heads/review/<N>), not the commit it built locally, because bus.sh confirm wants that tip (rule 23). Also: tools/audit/seat/tick_loop.sh relay_start (about lines 60-66) passes --confirm to cloud_relay.sh pass so a relayed verdict is posted with no hand step (assessor P15). Reviewed after #2547 and #2580, and after #2582 for tick_loop.sh. Also: cloud_relay.sh probe_arm writes .refused on every non-zero rc, so transient push failures are never retried; retry transients and log REFUSED <ref> <reason>.",
@@ -7042,7 +7044,8 @@
    "carry": [
     "add `carry_audit.py landed` (body item id present in its routed group's carry or brief at --roster-ref; CARRY-MISSING lines; rc 1) and `land-ops` (append-carry ops tagged `(items <ids>)`); bus.sh dispatch refuses on rc 1; fixtures are the #2558 pair (refuse, then pass after landing), the #2545 paraphrase (pass by id, a text-match mutant refuses), a dismissed item and a wrong-group id",
     "Lost-ask class, found 2026-10-20: fold (e) of #1955 was added by tvofi as an issue comment on 2026-10-04, written into the R9-SW-6 brief, and then dropped when #2006 implemented only (a)-(d) and closed the issue. The ask survived nowhere: not in the round-10 roster, not in an open issue, not in a pull-request carry. The class is an owner fold recorded on an issue rather than in the roster, so the issue's closure is what deletes it. Wanted: a fold count on the issue (a)-(e) that the closing pull request must answer item by item, and a check that a closing body naming fewer items than the issue's fold list refuses. The instance is now R10-THERMAL-POWER-OPTION on the roster.",
-    "`finding-propagation.md`: contradiction: the rule counts a roster carry as landed once it is on `handoff/audit-r10-roster`, but `pr-contract`'s carry step reads main's roster. Six pr-contract runs on this PR refused routings to groups the roster branch already held (`## Red checks`). The roster-sync step is `R10-ORCH-MACHINERY`'s. Carry text for the orchestrator to land: \"pr-contract's carry step and the rule must read the same roster; prepr or body_push should run carry_audit against the roster the check will read. (from #2545)\" Carry: R10-ORCH-MACHINERY"
