+    "Triage P-G (s4, 2026-10-23 07:10Z, accepted, narrowed), verbatim:\ncarry_audit resets a lead's inherited classification at a section-heading change. Failing test first: #2645's comment 6356993187 goes from 8 flagged to 1. A null control: a real block item written under a checklist heading still counts. Reject the heading allow-list form.\n\nMeasured facts: at origin/main tools/audit/carry_audit.py:204-207 a blocked verdict's item is flagged only by NONBLOCK in its text, a NONBLOCK-worded heading, LEAD, or inheritance. The real mechanism, measured by running items(text, True) on the round-1 blocked verdict of #2645 (origin/verdict/2645, cbac2180d, VERDICT.md): the paragraph \"Two more survivors. Neither blocks, but ...:\" is a flagged lead (:219-221 sets lead_flag), and lead_flag is cleared only by a non-bullet item (:192-193), never by a heading change. The sections after it hold fenced RESULT lines, the numbered \"Brief checklist\" and the \"Not re-derived\" bullets, so 7 of the 8 unrouted items are \"under lead\" and the 8th (item 5, \"Carries\") has a NONBLOCK word in its text. The cost: one park (run37) and one body patch.\nWhy the heading allow-list is unsound: it keys on heading names (\"Brief checklist\", \"Brief items\", \"Not re-derived\"), so it hides a real item a reviewer writes under such a heading, and any new heading name reopens it. The lead inheritance is the defect.\nFix: record the lead's section and clear lead_flag when an item's section differs from it. Measured on the same VERDICT.md: flagged items 8 to 1 (only item 5, a genuine NONBLOCK word). Bullets under the lead in its own section keep their prior classification.\nNull controls the fixer owes: (a) bullets under a lead in the SAME section still inherit; (b) a bullet carrying a LEAD or NONBLOCK word under a checklist heading still counts; (c) an item under a \"Block\" heading still counts; (d) the #2645 comment text gives 8 to at most 1.\nResidual: item 5-style false positives (a NONBLOCK word in a confirmation) stay; they cost a dismissal, not a park, and a word-level fix would be a second classifier. Decline it.\nCost: S, about 5-8 lines in items() plus 4-6 self-test rows (about 25 lines in total); check structure.py for carry_audit.py before the fixer starts. R10-FLOW-ROSTER-FREEZE also lists carry_audit.py but its brief is the roster freeze; keep the files apart."
